* Week 8: ARBNO(p) is ARB's growth-by-retry generalized to a whole
* subpattern -- `ARBNO(p) = NULL | p *ARBNO(p)` (research/snobol/
* 03-pattern-matching.md). ARBNO(ANY('AB')) against "ABABABC" tries
* zero repetitions first, then grows the run by one A/B character at a
* time on each backtrack. Because 'C' never occurs inside the leading
* run itself, every attempt shorter than all six A/B characters is
* doomed to fail the trailing 'C', so the search must grow all the way
* through the run -- shortest-first, not greedy -- before it succeeds.
        SUBJECT = 'ABABABC'
        SUBJECT ARBNO(ANY('AB')) 'C'   :F(NOMATCH)
        OUTPUT = 'ARBNO CONSUMED THE RUN'      :(STOP)
NOMATCH OUTPUT = 'NO MATCH'
STOP    SUBJECT = SUBJECT
